    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d585">

                <pb facs="1194" n="1154" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v09p1/pg1154"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">683.84A/3–1953: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 585<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Syria (Moose) to the
                        Department of State</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d585-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Damascus</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1953-03-19T16:00:00+02:00">March 19, 1953—4 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>601. According UNTSO, meeting March 16 Syrian and Israeli delegations discussed
                    northern and central zones but not southern zone since documentation on land
                    ownership not submitted (Embtel 592, March 12).<anchor n="2" xml:id="d585-f2"/>
                    Israelis confirmed willingness give up Dardara and land above Huleh necessary
                    compensate dispossessed central zone Arabs. MAC Chairman puzzled by
                    uncompromising attitude <pb facs="1195" n="1155" xml:id="pg1155"/> Syrians who
                    presented new demands such as for unlimited irrigation rights from upper Jordan
                    waters. Taxis endeavoring obtain appointments see Shishikli ascertain whether
                    Syrians changing position on zone settlement and to urge constructive attitude.
                    Date next MAC meeting not yet fixed.</p>
                <p>Taxis scheduled sail for US April 6. Apparently not yet decided who will replace
                    him on Syro-Israel MAC.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Moose</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d585-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d585-f1-content">
                <p>Repeated to Tel Aviv, Amman, Jerusalem, London, and Paris.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d585-f2" n="2" xml:id="d585-f2-content">
                <p>Telegram 592 from Damascus contained a report of the Syria-Israel meeting of Mar.
                    10. (683.84A/3–1253)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
